<title>BELGIUM: Fischler says member states slow to pay beef aid.</title>
<headline>Fischler says member states slow to pay beef aid.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Only two member states have so far paid emergency aid to beef producers although the deadline is October 15, Farm Commissioner Franz Fischler has told ministers.</p>
<p>Fischler told the farm Council on Tuesday it was therefore unrealistic to expect new measures to aid beef producers hit by the mad cow crisis to be implemented before the financial year ends in mid-october, Commission officials said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Fischler was responding to a French demand for extra aid for suckler cow farmers to be paid from the 1996 budget.</p>
<p>He added that member states had wide flexibility in using emergency funds and could provide extra national aid.</p>
<p>France has allocated most of the aid to beef finishers.</p>
<p>Other member states said extra aid should not be limited to suckler cows.</p>
</text>
